# Studio
Mode: Operate. Code-led. Decisions inferred under the user's explicit authorization; no interview, approval page, delegated agents or external models.

## Grounded directions, ordered by resonance
1. Polish school geometry textbook: clear sans, white, green diagrams; recognisable but familiar.
2. Botanical field guide: orderly captions, sage, branching forms; lets drawing lead.
3. Museum education workshop: pale sage furniture, precise dark ink, open white work surface, practical caption rhythm.
4. Transit wayfinding: compact labels, route colors, confident spatial grouping.
5. Children's science journal: warm paper, clear diagrams, friendly text.
6. Modernist educational poster: large geometric studies, restrained palette, bold hierarchy.
7. Library reference desk: quiet grey, strong indices, compact reference typography.

Assigned candidate 3 acknowledged. Challengers evaluated under the Operate limit (type, palette, density and one signature only): catalog declined (too much thumbnail density for writing), dance notation competitive on execution legibility but loses beginner identification; annual plate competitive on precision but loses educational familiarity; airline declined (status vocabulary foreign to coding); lexicon competitive for reference only; darkroom declined (low suitability to beginner drawing). Raises: catalog — make every example visibly identifiable by its actual geometry; notation — link execution line to turtle state; annual — exact shared alignment; airline — preserve draft history visibly; lexicon — reference entries carry executable examples; darkroom — support dark ambient work with a full theme.

THESIS: Write a small Polish command and see a precise, living geometric result.
OWN-WORLD: A museum education workshop. Pale sage shell #edf2ed, ink #253c34, white drawing field #ffffff, green #16866a, restrained apricot for learning notes. Familiar sans UI and actual monospaced code. No imitation paper texture.
STORY: Studio loads an executed rosette. Choose an example, inspect its code, change it, run or step; help and tasks stay one tab away. Drafts remain recoverable.
FIRST VIEWPORT: Compact branded header; workspace navigation; left program library with geometric thumbnails and a learning prompt; center numbered syntax-highlighted editor, run controls and current turtle state; right large dotted drawing field with mode tabs, pan/zoom/fit and lower coordinate status. Signature: each example thumbnail is rendered by the same interpreter and renderer as the main drawing.
FORM: seed:f39f069f5115ae8e. Three-area desktop workspace, stacked phone layout, precise 1px dividers, small consistent control radii, no decorative motion. Execution animates drawing and code together. Native keyboard buttons and semantic tabs.
